# Authoring + local-preview toolchain. Nothing here runs on Vercel: the site is static
# and every generated file (index.html's entries, finding/, llms.txt, sitemap.xml, the
# feeds) is built locally and committed. Keeping these out keeps the CDN bundle to
# exactly what is served.
#
# `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/`, and the difference is load-bearing: an excluded
# *directory* is never descended into, so a later negation inside it can never match and
# fails silently. Excluding the contents keeps the directory walkable, which is what lets
# the one exception below actually take effect.
scripts/*

# That exception: vercel.json's ignoreCommand runs this before a build to decide whether
# the push changed anything that is actually served, so it has to survive the line above
# and be on disk when Vercel looks for it.
!scripts/vercel-ignore-build.sh

# CI runs on GitHub, not Vercel.
.github/

# Repo docs, not site content.
README.md
docs/